Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore, WebCore: profile scopes for where a page's time goes

JSC::OBProfileScope calls the program's hooks (JSC::obProfileHooks) at
the begin and end of: compiling a script's or a function's code (parse and
bytecode: generateUnlinkedCodeBlockImpl, generateUnlinkedFunctionCodeBlock),
a script run from the top (JSExecState::profiledEvaluate), a call into
JavaScript (profiledCall: events, timers; with the called function's
script), a module's evaluation (linkAndEvaluateModule), a style update
(Document::resolveStyle) and a layout (LocalFrameViewLayoutContext::layout).
With no hooks set each scope costs a test. GFOpenBrowser's obcore-view
-profile sets them (src/webcore/ob_profile.cpp).

